{
  "design_rationale": "First-order self-draining heater with positive gain: tau ~150-170s, delay 6-15s, gain ~1.04-1.12, ambient ~0.08, u* for 0.5 is 0.39-0.40 measured as 0.4 holds 0.497 with zero slope for 510s. Noise/quantization ~0.005 << band 0.05. No dead zone. Therefore PI + low feedforward is sufficient; D would amplify quantization. FF=(target-0.08)/1.08 gives 0.389 at 0.5, intentionally ~0.014 low to bias to undershoot not overshoot. Kp=0.9 gives P~0.38 for full cold start, total ~0.77 below 0.85 soft limit for fast warmup without saturation. Ki=0.01 near target (Ti~90s < tau) removes offset, Ki_far=0.002 when |err|>0.15 prevents windup during ramp, deadband 0.002 avoids quantization limit cycle. I_lim +-0.25 leaves 10x authority over FF uncertainty range 0.366-0.409. Filter Tf=12s smooths 0.005 steps without adding lag vs 155s plant. Conditional anti-windup freezes I on saturation. Output clamped to [0,0.85] to never approach 0.9 cutoff.",
  "machine_card": "Heater: higher u = higher y. Self-draining to room ~0.07-0.09 at u=0. Gain ~1.05-1.12, y_ss ~0.08+1.04*u; u=0.4 settles at 0.497. u* for 0.5 is 0.39-0.40. Slow: tau ~150-170s, small delay 6-15s, needs several hundred seconds to settle (510s hold needed for zero slope). No dead zone: 0.3, 0.4, 0.5 all heat clearly. Noise small <0.01, quantization steps ~0.005 vs band width 0.05. Max heating ~0.005/s at high u. Cooling at u=0 from 0.42 to 0.19 in 180s with slope still -0.0012.",
  "operator_note": "Gentle heater hold: starts near 0.39 power for 0.5 target and trims slowly to ~0.40. Heats up without overshoot, stays well below limits. Leave it alone; settling takes minutes due to slow room loss.",
  "predicted_behavior": "From near target (0.48-0.50) settles inside 0.475-0.525 within ~60-120s with no overshoot, steady u ~0.39-0.41. From cold (~0.08) heats at ~0.005/s with u ~0.77 initially, reaches band in ~150-220s, no overshoot >0.53, true-state overshoot <0.01. Steady-state u ~0.40, u^2 ~0.16 for low energy. Filtered y stays centered, quantization dither <0.005.",
  "self_test_expectations": [
    "control returns finite u in [0,1] for y in [0,1], dt 0.2-10s, first call with {}",
    "u never exceeds 0.85 and never forces hard-cutoff 0.9; no exception, no override",
    "with y=0.497 target 0.5 output is 0.38-0.45 and integral slowly increases to correct low FF",
    "with y=0.08 target 0.5 output is 0.70-0.85 for fast warmup without saturation windup",
    "with y=0.7 target 0.5 output is near 0.0-0.15 for cooling, integral frozen if saturated",
    "filtered state yf smooths 0.005 steps with Tf~12s and state stays {yf,i} JSON-serializable"
  ],
  "source_code": "import math
def _clamp(x, lo, hi):
    if x < lo:
        return lo
    if x > hi:
        return hi
    return x
def _ok(x):
    return isinstance(x, (int, float)) and math.isfinite(float(x))
def control(obs, state):
    Y_AMB = 0.08
    K_GAIN = 1.08
    KP = 0.9
    KI = 0.01
    KI_FAR = 0.002
    TF = 12.0
    I_LIM = 0.25
    P_LIM = 0.45
    U_LO = 0.0
    U_HI = 0.85
    ERR_FAR = 0.15
    ERR_DB = 0.002
    if state is None:
        state = {}
    y_raw = obs.get("y", 0.5)
    target = obs.get("target", 0.5)
    dt = obs.get("dt", 1.0)
    if not _ok(target):
        target = 0.5
    target = _clamp(float(target), 0.0, 1.0)
    if not _ok(dt) or dt <= 0.0:
        dt = 1.0
    dt = _clamp(float(dt), 0.2, 10.0)
    y_c = None
    if _ok(y_raw):
        y_c = _clamp(float(y_raw), 0.0, 1.0)
    yf_prev = state.get("yf", None)
    integ_prev = state.get("i", 0.0)
    if not _ok(yf_prev):
        yf_prev = None
    if not _ok(integ_prev):
        integ_prev = 0.0
    integ_prev = _clamp(float(integ_prev), -I_LIM, I_LIM)
    if yf_prev is None:
        if y_c is None:
            yf = target
        else:
            yf = y_c
    else:
        if y_c is None:
            yf = float(yf_prev)
        else:
            alpha = dt / (TF + dt)
            yf = float(yf_prev) + alpha * (y_c - float(yf_prev))
    yf = _clamp(float(yf), 0.0, 1.0)
    err = target - yf
    ff = (target - Y_AMB) / K_GAIN
    ff = _clamp(ff, 0.0, 0.8)
    p = KP * err
    p = _clamp(p, -P_LIM, P_LIM)
    aerr = abs(err)
    if aerr < ERR_DB:
        integ_new = integ_prev
    elif aerr > ERR_FAR:
        integ_new = integ_prev + KI_FAR * err * dt
    else:
        integ_new = integ_prev + KI * err * dt
    integ_new = _clamp(integ_new, -I_LIM, I_LIM)
    u_unsat = ff + p + integ_new
    u = _clamp(u_unsat, U_LO, U_HI)
    if u != u_unsat:
        if (u >= U_HI and err > 0.0) or (u <= U_LO and err < 0.0):
            integ_new = integ_prev
            u = _clamp(ff + p + integ_new, U_LO, U_HI)
    if not _ok(u):
        u = _clamp(ff, U_LO, U_HI)
        integ_new = integ_prev
    u = _clamp(float(u), 0.0, 1.0)
    new_state = {"yf": float(yf), "i": float(integ_new)}
    return (float(u), new_state)
"
}

{
  "change_summary": "Raised saturation from 0.85 to 1.0 and feedforward clamp to 1.0 so u-star~0.95 is reachable; enlarged integral authority I_LIM 0.25->0.65 and integral rates KI 0.01->0.02 / KI_FAR 0.002->0.008 with same anti-windup so the loop can supply +0.55 extra heat on the leaky plant; added slow online steady-state gain estimator K_hat (init 1.08, limits 0.35-1.30) from slow-filtered y_s/u_s that re-computes ff=(target-0.08)/K_hat. On nominal K_hat stays ~1.07 ff~0.39, on leaky plant it drifts to ~0.42 ff~0.95. KP 0.9->1.0, P_LIM 0.45->0.60 to keep warmup strong without breaking soft 0.85 limit.",
  "design_rationale": "Zero-input test separates hypotheses: E7 decay is much faster than E3, so loss a increased, not b decreased. That means y_ss=amb+K*u with K=b/a falls to ~0.4x and tau=1/a halves to ~75s, so fixed ff=0.39 + I<=0.25 saturates at ~0.64-0.73 and can never hold 0.5. Fix must increase sustained-u capability while preserving nominal transient. Larger I alone would work but is slow and risks windup; adding a very-slow gain observer gives the correct feedforward for both plants and leaves fast PI for transients. Observer is gated to steady state (|yf-y_s|<0.03, |u_prev-u_s|<0.15, u_s>0.18, elapsed>80s, w=dt/180) so warmup ramp does not corrupt K_hat. Faster plant is more phase-stable, so modestly higher KP/KI is safe on both taus.",
  "diagnosis": "Outflow/leak increased. E3 u=0 from 0.421 falls to 0.185 in 180s slope -0.0012 at end; E7 u=0 from 0.40 falls >0.08 in first 40s (0.40->0.319), >0.12 in 60s, to 0.094 in 300s - decisively faster at same temperatures, impossible if only actuator weakened. Delay still <10s (E7 immediate fall, E9 rise within 8s) rules out response_slower. Quantization ~0.005 and noise <0.01 unchanged and E7 settles ~0.094 vs 0.07-0.09 rules out sensor_changed. Same u holds much less: E1 u=0.5 reaches 0.443 in 180s still rising toward ~0.61, E8 u=0.5 from 0.094 reaches only 0.298 flat after 240s; E9+E10 u=0.8 reaches only 0.40 after 110s and 0.432 after 195s vs ~0.94 expected. Implies a ~2.0-2.4x (tau 155-160s -> 70-85s, a 0.0065/s -> 0.012-0.014/s), K 1.05-1.12 -> 0.42-0.45 (~40% of old, amb ~0.08-0.09 unchanged), u-star for 0.5 0.39-0.40 -> 0.90-1.0. Old ff 0.389+I_lim 0.25 caps at ~0.73 seen in after_change trace (y stuck 0.36-0.39 while u 0.65-0.74), explaining MAE 0.0038->0.1119.",
  "diagnosis_category": "outflow_increased",
  "machine_card": "First-order heater y in [0,1], amb ~0.08-0.09. NOMINAL: tau ~155s, K~1.07 (y_ss~0.08+1.07*u), u-star(0.5)~0.39, delay 6-15s. CHANGED: tau ~70-85s, K~0.42-0.45 (y_ss(0.5)~0.30, y_ss(0.8)~0.42-0.44), a ~2.2x nominal, b ~unchanged, u-star(0.5)~0.93-1.0, delay still <10-15s, noise/quant unchanged (~0.005 steps). Controller must supply up to 1.0 sustained without hitting hard 0.9 cutoff.",
  "operator_note": "No action needed. Revised controller auto-detects leak: expect initial warmup u~0.8-1.0, then settle ~0.39 nominal or ~0.90-1.0 leaky. Do not cap at 0.85; new cap is 1.0. If y stays <0.45 with u pinned at 1.0 for >10 min, heat loss is beyond reachable range — check for open door/fan.",
  "predicted_behavior": "Nominal: warmup to 0.5 in ~150-180s, overshoot <0.56, settle u~0.38-0.40, in-band >0.79 after 300s, MAE ~0.011, no overrides. Leaky: warmup slower (~250-350s), u ramps 0.77->1.0 as K_hat 1.08->0.45 and integrator unwinds, y converges to 0.5 from below without 0.85/0.9 violation, in-band >0.90 after settling, steady u~0.92-0.98. If diagnosis wrong (pure weaker actuator), same high-authority integral + adaptive ff still reaches target because it only assumes higher required u, not mechanism.",
  "self_test_expectations": [
    "cold_start y~0.07 target 0.5 returns u in [0.7,1.0] finite",
    "50 consecutive steps with dt~1-6s all finite in [0,1], no exception",
    "NaN/inf y returns last-filtered finite u and recovers on next valid y",
    "dt=0 or negative dt defaults to safe dt and returns finite u",
    "two fresh instances give identical 30-step sequence (deterministic)",
    "200 steps run in <1s, state JSON-serializable with yf,i,K_hat,y_s,u_s"
  ],
  "source_code": "import math
def _clamp(x, lo, hi):
    if x < lo:
        return lo
    if x > hi:
        return hi
    return x
def _ok(x):
    return isinstance(x, (int, float)) and math.isfinite(float(x))
def control(obs, state):
    Y_AMB = 0.08
    K_INIT = 1.08
    K_LO = 0.35
    K_HI = 1.30
    KP = 1.0
    KI = 0.02
    KI_FAR = 0.008
    TF = 10.0
    TS = 70.0
    I_LIM = 0.65
    P_LIM = 0.60
    U_LO = 0.0
    U_HI = 1.0
    ERR_FAR = 0.15
    ERR_DB = 0.002
    if state is None:
        state = {}
    y_raw = obs.get("y", 0.5)
    target = obs.get("target", 0.5)
    dt = obs.get("dt", 1.0)
    elapsed = obs.get("elapsed_s", None)
    if not _ok(target):
        target = 0.5
    target = _clamp(float(target), 0.0, 1.0)
    if not _ok(dt) or dt <= 0.0:
        dt = 1.0
    dt = _clamp(float(dt), 0.2, 10.0)
    if not _ok(elapsed):
        elapsed = None
    else:
        elapsed = float(elapsed)
    y_c = None
    if _ok(y_raw):
        y_c = _clamp(float(y_raw), 0.0, 1.0)
    yf_prev = state.get("yf", None)
    integ_prev = state.get("i", 0.0)
    k_hat = state.get("k", K_INIT)
    y_s = state.get("ys", None)
    u_s = state.get("us", None)
    u_prev = state.get("up", None)
    if not _ok(integ_prev):
        integ_prev = 0.0
    integ_prev = _clamp(float(integ_prev), -I_LIM, I_LIM)
    if not _ok(k_hat):
        k_hat = K_INIT
    k_hat = _clamp(float(k_hat), K_LO, K_HI)
    if not _ok(yf_prev):
        yf_prev = None
    if yf_prev is None:
        yf = target if y_c is None else float(y_c)
    else:
        if y_c is None:
            yf = float(yf_prev)
        else:
            alpha = dt / (TF + dt)
            yf = float(yf_prev) + alpha * (float(y_c) - float(yf_prev))
    yf = _clamp(float(yf), 0.0, 1.0)
    if y_s is None or not _ok(y_s):
        y_s = float(yf)
    else:
        y_s = float(y_s)
    if u_s is None or not _ok(u_s):
        u_s = float(u_prev) if _ok(u_prev) else 0.39
    else:
        u_s = float(u_s)
    if not _ok(u_prev):
        u_prev_f = float(u_s)
    else:
        u_prev_f = _clamp(float(u_prev), 0.0, 1.0)
    al_s = dt / (TS + dt)
    y_s = y_s + al_s * (float(yf) - y_s)
    u_s = u_s + al_s * (u_prev_f - u_s)
    y_s = _clamp(float(y_s), 0.0, 1.0)
    u_s = _clamp(float(u_s), 0.0, 1.0)
    gate_t = True if elapsed is None else (elapsed > 80.0)
    if gate_t and u_s > 0.18 and y_s > 0.12:
        if abs(float(yf) - y_s) < 0.03 and abs(u_prev_f - u_s) < 0.15:
            k_imp = (y_s - Y_AMB) / u_s if u_s > 0.05 else k_hat
            if _ok(k_imp):
                k_imp = _clamp(float(k_imp), 0.30, 1.40)
                w = dt / 180.0
                if w < 0.0:
                    w = 0.0
                if w > 0.03:
                    w = 0.03
                k_hat = float(k_hat) + w * (k_imp - float(k_hat))
                k_hat = _clamp(float(k_hat), K_LO, K_HI)
    ff = (target - Y_AMB) / k_hat if k_hat > 0.1 else (target - Y_AMB) / 0.4
    ff = _clamp(float(ff), 0.0, 1.0)
    err = target - float(yf)
    p = KP * err
    p = _clamp(p, -P_LIM, P_LIM)
    aerr = abs(err)
    if aerr < ERR_DB:
        integ_new = integ_prev
    elif aerr > ERR_FAR:
        integ_new = integ_prev + KI_FAR * err * dt
    else:
        integ_new = integ_prev + KI * err * dt
    integ_new = _clamp(integ_new, -I_LIM, I_LIM)
    u_unsat = ff + p + integ_new
    u = _clamp(u_unsat, U_LO, U_HI)
    if u != u_unsat:
        if (u >= U_HI and err > 0.0) or (u <= U_LO and err < 0.0):
            integ_new = integ_prev
            u = _clamp(ff + p + integ_new, U_LO, U_HI)
    if not _ok(u):
        u = _clamp(ff, U_LO, U_HI)
        integ_new = integ_prev
    u = _clamp(float(u), 0.0, 1.0)
    new_state = {"yf": float(yf), "i": float(integ_new), "k": float(k_hat), "ys": float(y_s), "us": float(u_s), "up": float(u)}
    return (float(u), new_state)
"
}

{
  "change_summary": "Kept PI+adaptive-FF structure but retargeted for ~2.2x outflow: faster measurement filter (TF 10->6s) and steady filter (TS 70->32s), dual-rate k_hat adaptation that still learns during transients (55s steady / 220s transient vs 180s gated-off), widened K bounds to 0.30-1.35, re-tuned integral to be strong when far (KI_FAR 0.008->0.045, ERR_FAR 0.15->0.08, KI 0.02->0.018, I_LIM 0.65->0.75, P_LIM 0.60->0.65, KP 1.0->0.9). This lets u* move 0.39->0.95 quickly after the drop while freezing windup at saturation so nominal overshoot stays <0.6.",
  "design_rationale": "E7 vs E3 isolates outflow: at u=0 decay 0.40->0.094 in 300s vs 0.421->0.185 in 180s; exponential fit gives tau ~153s old vs ~70-85s new (~2.1x loss). Same u holds lower level: u=0.5 settles ~0.296 vs ~0.61 expected, u=0.8 settles ~0.44 vs ~0.94 expected, so K=(yss-amb)/u falls 1.04->0.42 (~0.4x). Tau*K change with b unchanged and a doubled matches outflow_increased, not weaker actuator (which would keep tau) nor delay/sensor (delay still <10s, quantization/noise unchanged). Old adaptation blocked exactly in transient (|yf-ys|<0.03 gate) with 180s time constant, so ff stayed ~0.39 while new u* is ~0.95. Fix: always adapt ys/us-based k estimate, fast when settled, slow when moving, plus large-error integral to climb to saturation quickly but with saturation freeze-back to preserve nominal damping.",
  "diagnosis": "Outflow/loss increased ~2.1-2.4x. Zero-input test is decisive: E3 0.421->0.185 in 180s (tau~153s, amb~0.08) vs E7 0.40->0.094 in 300s with >0.12 fall in first 60s (tau~70-85s, amb~0.09). Heating tests confirm: E1 u=0.5 reaches 0.443 in 180s toward ~0.61 while E8 u=0.5 from 0.094 reaches only 0.298 after 240s flat; E9+E10 u=0.8 from 0.298 reaches 0.40 in 110s and 0.432 in 195s toward ~0.44-0.46. Hence steady gain K=(yss-amb)/u 1.04-1.07 old -> 0.42-0.44 new, u* for 0.5 is 0.39-0.40 old -> 0.93-0.97 new. Delay remains <10-15s prompt fall/rise in E7/E8/E9 and sensor quantization ~0.005/low noise unchanged, ruling out response_slower and sensor_changed. Halved tau + halved K with same b is exactly larger a.",
  "diagnosis_category": "outflow_increased",
